{
  "headline": "FDA's records show Takeda Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. posted a discontinuation for carbamazepine extended-release capsules on 2025-12-19; our supply traces to Northstar Rx LLC product labeled by Umedica Laboratories Pvt. Ltd. (FEI 3008460260) with VAI inspections through 2024-03-29",
  "headline_cites": ["E8", "E7", "E6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows Takeda Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. posted a discontinuation for carbamazepine capsule, extended release on 2025-12-19 with status To Be Discontinued.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East and Corvale General both carry carbamazepine extended-release tablets under NDC 72603088701 labeled by Northstar Rx LLC with SPL set ID b563e4a1-d7dd-4901-ad45-614f85687589.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label identifies Umedica Laboratories Pvt. Ltd. (FEI 3008460260) as the registered plant for manufacture and analysis.",
      "cites": ["E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for FEI 3008460260 show VAI classifications on 2015-10-09, 2019-07-05, and 2024-03-29 with no OAI classification recorded.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 9 days on hand at current use and Corvale General has 20 days on hand, so a transfer of 37 units from Corvale General to Corvale East would bring Corvale East to about 14 days on hand while Corvale General remains above two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the links between the Takeda discontinuation and our Northstar-sourced supply are weak and no FDA cause is stated for this NDC, verify whether the Northstar product is affected by any separate supply constraint or allocation.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E1", "E2"]
    }
  ]
}
